  "summary": "Hi, I'm Eli Lopez, a Computer Science graduate from San Diego State University with a strong passion for software engineering, system design, and building solutions that make an impact.\n\nDuring my five years as a server and trainer at P.F. Chang’s, I developed skills that complement my technical abilities: communication, teamwork, leadership, problem-solving under pressure, and a deep commitment to delivering quality results. I balanced this role while being a full-time CS student, which strengthened my discipline, time management, and work ethic.\n\nIn school and personal projects, I’ve built systems involving multithreading, scheduling algorithms, data structures, concurrency, memory management, and C/C++ development. I enjoy breaking down complex problems, writing clean and efficient code, and continually learning new technologies.\n\nI’m currently looking for an opportunity as a Software Engineer, where I can contribute, grow, and bring both my technical background and people first mindset to a team.",
